========================================================================
Blazor WASM Standalone (.NET 10) + Web API + Keycloak-Login
mit FluentUI-Username oben rechts
========================================================================


------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. NUGET-PAKETE
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Authentication
Microsoft.FluentUI.AspNetCore.Components


------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. PROGRAM.CS
------------------------------------------------------------------------

builder.Services.AddOidcAuthentication(options =>
{
    builder.Configuration.Bind("Oidc", options.ProviderOptions);
    options.ProviderOptions.ResponseType = "code"; // PKCE
    // Wichtig fuer Username-Claim aus Keycloak:
    options.UserOptions.NameClaim = "preferred_username";
});
builder.Services.AddFluentUIComponents();


------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. wwwroot/appsettings.json
------------------------------------------------------------------------

{
  "Oidc": {
    "Authority": "https://keycloak.example.com/realms/DEIN_REALM",
    "ClientId": "blazor-wasm",
    "ResponseType": "code",
    "DefaultScopes": [ "openid", "profile", "email" ]
  }
}


------------------------------------------------------------------------
4. KEYCLOAK-CLIENT-KONFIGURATION
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Im Keycloak-Admin fuer den Client "blazor-wasm":

  - Access Type: public
  - Standard Flow enabled: on (Authorization Code + PKCE)
  - Valid Redirect URIs:
        https://deine-app/authentication/login-callback
  - Valid Post Logout Redirect URIs:
        https://deine-app/authentication/logout-callback
        <-- fehlt meist, wenn Logout nicht geht!
  - Web Origins: +  (oder deine Origin explizit)


------------------------------------------------------------------------
5. LOGOUT-PROBLEM
------------------------------------------------------------------------

Logout scheitert bei Keycloak fast immer an zwei Dingen:

a) Post-Logout-Redirect-URI nicht registriert (siehe Punkt 4).

b) Keycloak verlangt bei OIDC-Logout je nach Version den
   id_token_hint. Die Standard-RemoteAuthenticatorView macht das
   korrekt, wenn du sie einbindest.

In neueren Keycloak-Versionen (18+) ist der Endpoint
   /protocol/openid-connect/logout
und erfordert entweder id_token_hint ODER
client_id + post_logout_redirect_uri.

Bei Problemen: Browser-Konsole / Network-Tab auf die genaue
Fehlermeldung pruefen.


------------------------------------------------------------------------
6. Authentication.razor
------------------------------------------------------------------------

@page "/authentication/{action}"
@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.WebAssembly.Authentication

<RemoteAuthenticatorView Action="@Action" />

@code {
    [Parameter] public string? Action { get; set; }
}


------------------------------------------------------------------------
7. MainLayout.razor  (Username oben rechts mit FluentUI)
------------------------------------------------------------------------

@using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization

<FluentLayout>
    <FluentHeader>
        <span>Meine App</span>
        <FluentSpacer />
        <AuthorizeView>
            <Authorized>
                <FluentStack Orientation="Orientation.Horizontal"
                             VerticalAlignment="VerticalAlignment.Center">
                    <FluentPersona Name="@context.User.Identity?.Name"
                                   ImageSize="32px" />
                    <FluentButton Appearance="Appearance.Stealth"
                                  @onclick="BeginLogout">Abmelden</FluentButton>
                </FluentStack>
            </Authorized>
            <NotAuthorized>
                <FluentButton @onclick="BeginLogin">Anmelden</FluentButton>
            </NotAuthorized>
        </AuthorizeView>
    </FluentHeader>
    <FluentBodyContent>@Body</FluentBodyContent>
</FluentLayout>

@code {
    [Inject] NavigationManager Nav { get; set; } = default!;
    void BeginLogin()  => Nav.NavigateToLogin("authentication/login");
    void BeginLogout() => Nav.NavigateToLogout("authentication/logout");
}


------------------------------------------------------------------------
8. HINWEISE
------------------------------------------------------------------------

- context.User.Identity?.Name liefert den Wert des NameClaim
  (preferred_username) - also den AD-Benutzernamen, wenn Keycloak
  per LDAP/AD foederiert ist.

- App.razor muss in CascadingAuthenticationState gewrappt sein.

- _Imports.razor sollte enthalten:
      @using Microsoft.AspNetCore.Components.Authorization

